BUG: in `fn step_for_record(&mut self, value: &Value) -> Option<RpcStep>` (about line 248) the injected mapper's `RpcMapping { events, finished, ended_aborted }` is handled as:
    if mapping.ended_aborted { self.ended_aborted = true; }
    if mapping.finished { let aborted = self.ended_aborted; self.run_active = false; self.prompt_id = None; self.ended_aborted = false; return Some(RpcStep::RunFinished { aborted }); }
    if !mapping.events.is_empty() { return Some(RpcStep::Events(mapping.events)); }
    None
so when ONE record both carries events AND finishes the run (Claude's `result` message maps to a usage UpdateEvent plus finished=true), the events are silently DROPPED. Pi never hit it because its finishing record has no events.

FIX (exact): add a private field `deferred_finish: Option<bool>` to `RpcSession` (the bool is the `aborted` flag; initialise it to None in `new`). In step_for_record, change the finished branch to: 
    if mapping.finished {
        let aborted = self.ended_aborted;
        if mapping.events.is_empty() { /* unchanged: do the bookkeeping above and return RunFinished immediately */ }
        else { self.deferred_finish = Some(aborted); return Some(RpcStep::Events(mapping.events)); }   // run_active/prompt_id/ended_aborted stay as they are until the deferred finish is delivered
    }
and at the TOP of `pub fn next_step`, right AFTER the existing `if self.exited { ... return RpcStep::Exited; }` block and BEFORE `let deadline = ...`, add:
    if let Some(aborted) = self.deferred_finish.take() { self.run_active = false; self.prompt_id = None; self.ended_aborted = false; return RpcStep::RunFinished { aborted }; }
(So a finishing record with events yields Events(..) first, then RunFinished on the very next call.) Also, if `JsonlRecord::Exited` or an Error arrives while a finish is deferred, nothing special is needed because the deferred finish is delivered first on the next call.
Update the doc comments of next_step/RpcStep::RunFinished minimally if they claim a finishing record never carries events.

